<title>NEW ZEALAND: BNZ to launch new index-tracking retail fund.</title>
<headline>BNZ to launch new index-tracking retail fund.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of New Zealand said on Tuesday it will launch a new index-tracking retail investment fund, named &quot;BNZ 25&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;The current tax environment and the need for certainty around long-term saving in New Zealand are issues closely linked to the new fund,&quot; BNZ said.</p>
<p>The bank said it would hold a media briefing at 3.15 p.m. on Wednesday to discuss the new fund and related issues, and declined to give any further details until then.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
